' 23 The crossed stacks of the M-1 arbitration: why a pop must bump the
' collection counter of a stack.
'
' Source of a figure for the P5 merge section of ../verification.md (and of
' design.md section N3). The figure restates the headline
' crossed_stacks_without_removal_counters_fabricate of
' formal/rocq/reified_rspaces/theories/CounterConflict.v, the Unsafe control
' RemovalCounterFreeUnsafe.cfg of CounterConflict.tla, and the test
' space_collection_conflicts_crossed_stacks of
' rholang/tests/reified_merge_p5.rs. It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order, from the top to the bottom:
'   1. The pre-state: the stack a holds 10 and the stack b holds 20. Each
'      stack has a counter record.
'   2. Branch A pushes 1 onto a and pops b. Branch B pushes 2 onto b and
'      pops a.
'   3. Lane 1 (the code): every operation bumps its counter, so the branches
'      consume the same counter produces of a and b. Check #1 reports a
'      race, and the merge rejects one branch.
'   4. Lane 2 (a pop without a counter bump): the branches consume
'      different produces, so no check fires. The merge keeps both pops, but
'      each serial order gives another pop.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 23-crossed-stacks-merge.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 23-crossed-stacks-merge
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $ca_note_amber
skinparam PartitionBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
title The crossed stacks: a pop must bump the counter (plan revision M-1)

start
:pre-state of two stack collections:
the stack a holds 10 and the stack b holds 20,
with the counter records <latex>S(\mathit{sid}, a)</latex> and <latex>S(\mathit{sid}, b)</latex>; <<$rrs_storage>>
split
  :branch A, one deploy:
  push 1 onto a, pop b (the top record 20); <<$rrs_agent>>
split again
  :branch B, one deploy:
  push 2 onto b, pop a (the top record 10); <<$rrs_agent>>
end split
split
  partition "Lane 1: the code" {
    :every operation bumps its counter (decision 31):
    A and B both consume the pre-state counter
    produces of a and of b, in COMMs without peeks; <<$rrs_agent>>
    :check #1: the consumed sets share
    both counter produces; <<$rrs_host>>
    :race on both counters: the merge rejects one branch
    (crossed_collections_race); <<$rrs_reject>>
  }
split again
  partition "Lane 2: no pop bump" {
    :a pop does not bump the counter (RemovalCounterFree):
    A consumes the counter produce of a and the record 20.
    B consumes the counter produce of b and the record 10; <<$rrs_agent>>
    :checks #1, #2 and #3 find nothing; <<$rrs_host>>
    :the merge keeps both pops:
    A popped 20 and B popped 10; <<$rrs_storage>>
    split
      :serial order A, then B:
      B pops 1, the push of A; <<$rrs_reject>>
    split again
      :serial order B, then A:
      A pops 2, the push of B; <<$rrs_reject>>
    end split
    :no serial order gives the merged outcome
    (crossed_stacks_without_removal_counters_fabricate); <<$rrs_reject>>
  }
end split
stop

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_storage>    | stored state: the records and the merged outcome |
|<$rrs_agent>      | space operation of a deploy, with its counter bumps |
|<$rrs_host>       | merger of the baseline, unchanged |
|<$rrs_reject>     | a rejected branch, or an outcome that no serial order gives |
endlegend
@enduml
